<title>USA: Bell Boeing Tiltrotor wins contract.</title>
<headline>Bell Boeing Tiltrotor wins contract.</headline>
<dateline>ARLINGTON, Va 1997-01-06</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Bell Boeing Tiltrotor Team said Monday it had won a $490-million contract from the U.S. Navy to make improvements to one of its helicopter models.  </p>
<p>The company said it would add special operational features to the craft like navigational and communications equipment to the CV-22, which is a variant of the Osprey model.</p>
<p>The helicopter is used by the special operations forces of the U.S. Naval Air Systems Command.</p>
<p>The company said it would also remake the MV-22 EMD aircraft No. 9.</p>
</text>
